# CKD Prediction Web App

A Machine Learning-based web application developed to predict the possibility of Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) using selected clinical parameters.

## 1. Project Overview

The CKD Prediction Web App is a Flask-based Machine Learning application that allows users to enter patient clinical information and obtain a CKD prediction using a trained Machine Learning model.

The application also provides user authentication, patient record management, prediction results, and PDF report generation.

This project demonstrates the integration of Machine Learning, Python, Flask, database management, and frontend web technologies into a single application.

---

## 2. Problem Statement

Chronic Kidney Disease can develop gradually and may not always show noticeable symptoms during its early stages.

The purpose of this project is to develop a web application that uses Machine Learning to analyse selected clinical parameters and provide a CKD prediction.

The application is intended for educational and demonstration purposes.

---

## 3. Objectives

The main objectives of this project are:

- To develop a Machine Learning model for CKD prediction.
- To create a user-friendly web application using Flask.
- To allow users to enter patient clinical information.
- To integrate the trained Machine Learning model with the web application.
- To store patient information and prediction results.
- To provide downloadable PDF reports.
- To demonstrate the practical use of Machine Learning in a web application.

---

## 4. Technologies Used

| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Python | Application and Machine Learning development |
| Flask | Web application framework |
| Flask-SQLAlchemy | Database integration |
| Flask-Migrate | Database migration management |
| Flask-Mail | Email functionality |
| Pandas | Data processing |
| Scikit-learn | Machine Learning |
| Joblib | Saving and loading the trained model |
| HTML | Web page structure |
| CSS | Web page styling |
| JavaScript | Frontend functionality |
| SQLite | Database |

---

## 5. Machine Learning

The application uses a trained Machine Learning model stored in:

`model.pkl`

The model uses the following clinical parameters:

- Age
- Blood Pressure
- Specific Gravity
- Albumin
- Sugar
- Blood Glucose
- Blood Urea
- Serum Creatinine
- Hemoglobin
- Hypertension
- Diabetes Mellitus
- Anemia

The Flask application loads the trained model and uses the entered clinical parameters to generate a prediction.

---

## 6. Dataset

The project contains the preprocessed dataset:

`CKD_Preprocessed.csv`

The dataset contains clinical parameters used for Machine Learning development.

The preprocessing stage prepares the data in a suitable format for training and prediction.

---

## 7. System Workflow

Patient Information
        ↓
Web Form
        ↓
Flask Application
        ↓
Data Processing
        ↓
Machine Learning Model
        ↓
CKD Prediction
        ↓
Prediction Result
        ↓
Patient Record / PDF Report
